   1.  An Introduction
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   UserList  was  written because I recently decided to upgrade my BBS to
   Excelsior!   BBS.   I had originally written UserList for Falcon CBCS,
   and when I upgraded, I needed the same sort of program.  And seeing as
   the  UserData  files are totally different, I had to re-write UserList
   from the bottom up.




   2.  Requirments
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   UserList can be used on any Amiga, and does not require Excelsior!  to
   be  running  to  work.   But  it does require a valid UserData file to
   work.

   The  way  UserList determins of the selected file is a likely UserData
   file is by dividing the file size by 1268 (the size of an account), so
   the chances of UserList working with a wrong file is pretty slim.




   3.  Usage
   ~~~~~~~~~
   UserList can be used from the CLI/SHELL or from the workbench.  If run
   from  the  workbench,  a  file  requestor  will  be  presented to you,
   allowing  you  to select the UserData file to examine.  A small window
   will  be  opened  to  display  the  text (this is via CONSOLE:) At the
   moment,  you  cannot  make any modifications to the first/last user or
   the access level to view.


   When run from the shell, the arguments available are:

     FILENAME/A,FIRST/K/N,LAST/K/N,E=EXTEND/S,ACCESS/K,CALLS/K,A=ALIAS/K,
     N=NAME/K,C=COMPUTER/K,P=PLACE/K

     FILENAME  - This is the name of the UserData file to display.  There
                 is   no   default   file.    If   none  is  provided,  a
                 filerequester  will  be  generated.   If no file is then
                 selected,  then  UserList  will  exit without displaying
                 anything.


     FIRST     - This allows you to specify which  user number  is to the
                 first displayed.  This can be handy if you have a lot of
                 users,  and just want to see who is new(ish).  The FIRST
                 keyword  must be present for this function to work.
                 eg.  FIRST=40 would display all users after #40.


     LAST      - Similar  to  FIRST,  but  specifies the last entry to be
                 displayed.   The  LAST  keyword must be present for this
                 function  to work.  eg.  LAST=40 would display all users
                 before #40.


     ACCESS    - This allows you to only view users of one certain level.
                 The  ACCESS keyword must be present for this function to
                 work.  eg.  if you wanted to see who the new users were,
                 you would use something like:  ACCESS=1.

                 There  is  a  "or  higher"  than option on this entry as
                 well.   If you place an 'H' after the access level, then
                 all  users  of  that  level or higher will be shown.
                 eg.  ACCESS=10H will show all users of access 10 or up.


     CALLS     - This is part of the exended information, but can be used
                 to find out all users who have called x number of times.
                 Simply  enter  the  keyword  (CALLS=)  and the number of
                 calls you want to match it against, and only those users
                 that have called that many times will be displayed.

                 As  with ACCESS there is a "or higher" option.  Just put
                 a 'H' after the number of calls, and all users that have
                 called  more  than or equal to the number will be shown.
                 eg.  CALLS=30H will show all users that have called more
                 than 30 times.


     EXTEND    - When  this keyword is present, extra information will be
                 typed  on  the line below the main line.  At the moment,
                 this  is  the users phone number, and number of calls to
                 the system.


     ALIAS     - The users alias
     NAME      - The users real name
     COMPUTER  - Type of computer
     PLACE     - Where they are calling from

                 These are all keywords for data matching.  They all work
                 the same way, but affect different entries.  The routine
                 is case insensitive, and allows partial matches.

                 If  you  wanted  to  list  all users with a real name of
                 David  and  owned  an  Amiga,  then  you  might  use the
                 following two options:

                               NAME=David COMPUTER=amiga

                 To include a space, enclose the option in quotes (")
                 eg.  "ALIAS=The Boss"




   4.  Shareware and Registration
   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
   Due  to  the  VERY  poor  response  that  I recived over several other
   utilities  that I wrote and released, and KNOW people use, I have been
   forced to "restrict" usage of my programs.

   Therefore,  when  you run UserList, and you do not have a keyfile from
   me,  then  there  will  be  a  5 second delay after startup before the
   information  display  begins.   Also, the 'EXTEND' option (which shows
   extra information about the user) is DISABLED.

   I am sorry to be so harsh, but I at least want to know that people are
   using things I write and value my time enough to say hello.


   Also, due to the fact that UserList isn't the sort of program that you
   are  going  to  use  every waking moment of everyday, the KeyFile that
   will be mailed to you when you register will also work with most of my
   other utilties.

   I  look forward to seeing all these letters/EMail's coming in from all
   the Excelsior SysOp's out there.




   5.  History
   ~~~~~~~~~~~
   V1.0  Unknown 92
       * First release.  Written in assembly for Falcon CBCS

   V2.0  20 February 93
       * Rewrote in E for use with Excelsior! BBS

   V2.1  21 February 93
       * Added FIRST/LAST user options
       * Added show only one level option (ACCESS)
       * Rewrote file handler to provide decent error reporting
       * Made minor changes to speed things up a bit

   V2.2  22 February 93
       * Added HIGHER option.

   V2.21 22 February 93
       * Corrected error that prevented  anything from being typed unless
         either the HIGHER or ACCESS options were selected.
       * Decreased  check loop by  one.  Now scans for the correct number
         of users only.

   V2.3  7 March 93
       * Changed code  to work with new Version1  userdata file  (used by
         Excelsior! versions 0.979+)
       * Added EXTEND option.  Now shows Phone number and number of calls
       * Added options to match data with entries for Name,  Alias, City,
         Computer, number of calls

   V2.4   13 March 93
       * Fixed a couple of minor bugs
       * Improved processing speed of data
       * Added Keyfile restrictions




